        <p style="font-size:0.92rem;color:#2a3c54;line-height:1.73;margin:0 0 14px">Yes. If the cause turns out to be a clogged filter, a coin or sock jammed in the impeller, or a hose installation issue, the repair can be considerably simpler and less expensive.</p>
        <p style="font-size:0.92rem;color:#2a3c54;line-height:1.73;margin:0 0 14px">On this unit, those causes were ruled out before the pump was replaced. That matters because we do not replace parts based on the symptom alone.</p>
        <div style="padding:14px 20px;background:rgba(176,22,22,0.05);border-left:3px solid #dc2626;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0">
          <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:#1a2c44;line-height:1.6;margin:0;font-style:italic;font-weight:600">Diagnosis comes before parts.</p>
        </div>
