        </h2>
        <p style="font-size:0.92rem;color:#2a3c54;line-height:1.73;margin:0 0 14px">At $353.18, repairing an otherwise serviceable front-load washer can make good financial sense compared with replacing it. Replacing a comparable Samsung front-loader can cost substantially more.</p>
        <p style="font-size:0.92rem;color:#2a3c54;line-height:1.73;margin:0 0 14px">The answer is not always repair. It would be a different conversation if the machine also had severe bearing noise, a damaged drum, repeated expensive failures, or significant control board issues. That was not the situation here.</p>
        <p style="font-size:0.92rem;color:#2a3c54;line-height:1.73;margin:0">On this service call, the confirmed failure was the drain pump. The washer had no other diagnosed problems. Once the pump was replaced and drain and spin were verified, the repair was done.</p>
